{%- comment -%}
  One declared directory's README. Rendered by `subgraph-readmes` into the
  `kg:subgraph` marker region of `<directory>/README.md`.

  Every value comes from the Knowledge Graph:
    subgraph  the directory's declaration entry (id, path, title,
              description, kinds) — `kg.directories[]` in the declaration
    instance  the declaring instance (name, title, readme: a relative link)
    release   its version, and for an instance declaring an iriBase its
              release addresses: version, major, agent (<iriBase><version>/,
              for what a program reads), human (<iriBase>v<major>/, for
              pages). Empty strings where not declared — never a typed number.
    kg        the whole declaration, for any field a template wants
    files     each file directly here: path, what (read from the file),
              usedBy (from diagrams that name it)
    subdirs   each subdirectory: name, count, readme (a link, or empty)
    process   the DECLARED governing process (`coverage.process`), resolved
              to its diagram and its rendered SVG — or nil when the directory
              declares none, which is an answer and not a gap
{%- endcomment -%}
